children.text:
Am I like a cattle-lifter, a stalwart person? This is no task for me: rather I care
        for other things: I care for sleep, and milk of my mother's breast, and wrappings round my
        shoulders, and warm baths. Let no one hear the cause of this dispute;

and over dogs and all flocks that the wide earth nourishes, and over all sheep;
        also that he only should be the appointed messenger to Hades, who, though he takes no gift,
        shall give him no mean prize.
